 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? That's the paint sitting on top of the layer below disappearing. The dryer the paint, the more the shadows grow. You can slow it down by varnishing sooner and several coats rather than one thick one. Yes, mix a small test area with one layer of thick paint and see how dark it gets. If it' too much, thin the bottom layer with paint thinner. Use gloss paint over the top. Gloss hides shadows better than matte or silk.",
